<section id="1000Y_S0012" variety="S0012">
<name>SRS Airbag</name>
<ttl id="1000Y_S0012_745Q2_T00B8" variety="T00B8">
<name>SRS Airbag System</name>
<para id="RM000002T0P003X" category="C" type-id="801OV" name-id="554GL-00" from="200612" to="200912">
<dtccode>B1602</dtccode>
<dtcname>Driver side front satellite sensor bus communication stop</dtcname>
<dtccode>B1603</dtccode>
<dtcname>Driver Side Front Satellite Sensor Bus Initialization Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>B1612</dtccode>
<dtcname>Front airbag sensor RH communication stop</dtcname>
<dtccode>B1613</dtccode>
<dtcname>Front airbag sensor RH initialization malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002T0P003X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000068D00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The front airbag sensor RH circuit consists of the airbag computer assembly and front airbag sensor RH. </ptxt>
<ptxt>The front airbag sensor RH detects impacts and sends signals to the airbag computer assembly to determine whether to deploy the airbags. </ptxt>
<ptxt>When a malfunction is detected in the front airbag sensor RH circuit, DTCs B1602, B1603, B1612 and B1613 are stored in the airbag computer assembly. </ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Trouble Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B1602</ptxt>
<ptxt>B1603</ptxt>
<ptxt>B1612</ptxt>
<ptxt>B1613</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Open, short between terminals, short to +B or short to ground in the wire harness between the airbag computer assembly and front airbag sensor RH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Front airbag sensor RH malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly Malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Front Airbag Sensor RH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument panel wire (between airbag computer assembly and junction connector)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine room main wire (between junction connector and front airbag sensor RH)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002T0P003X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000068E00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C159565J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002T0P003X_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002T0P003X_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000002T0P003X_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000068F00000">
<testtitle>Connector Inspection</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait for 90 seconds.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Make sure the ignition switch is OFF before disconnecting the cable from the negative (-) battery terminal.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the connection condition of the connectors connected to the airbag computer assembly and front airbag sensor RH, and of the junction connectors (engine room main wire and instrument panel wire).</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The connector is connected properly </ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the connectors connected to the airbag computer assembly and front airbag sensor RH, and the junction connectors (engine room main wire and instrument panel wire), and check the condition of the terminals of each connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The terminals are not deformed or damaged</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T0P003X_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T0P003X_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T0P003X_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___000068G00000">
<testtitle>Front Airbag Sensor RH Circuit Short to Ground Inspection (Between Airbag Computer Assembly and Front Airbag Sensor RH)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect junction connectors C and D.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C101084J11" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal of connector B and body ground.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1-29 (+SR) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1M Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1-27 (-SR) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1M Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T0P003X_04_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T0P003X_04_0012" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T0P003X_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___000068H00000">
